+		/*
+		 * cpu_spc is deliberately left unreferenced. Standalone power
+		 * collapse and Krait frequency switching wedge cores when they
+		 * run together: a core that is collapsed while the shared
+		 * cpufreq policy reprograms its mux and HFPLL does not come
+		 * back, and stops answering even an NMI. Measured 2026-09-11 --
+		 * with the frequency pinned, 35k collapses under load over 20
+		 * minutes are fine; with it moving, 2832 transitions killed the
+		 * machine. Dropping the reference leaves the SPM cpuidle driver
+		 * with no DT state, so it does not register and idle falls back
+		 * to plain WFI. Restore the four "cpu-idle-states" properties
+		 * once the switching path is made safe against a collapsed core.
+		 */
